      "topic": "background",
      "summary": "Warm-season fruiting crop with determinate and indeterminate habits. Chilling affects growth and reproduction; frost damages exposed tissues. Excessive heat can reduce pollen function and fruit set; night and day exposure have different effects. Other Solanaceae can share some pathogens; resistant cultivars or grafting do not automatically remove rotation risk. Protected and open-field calendars differ; first ripe fruit and final harvest are different cycle endpoints.",
